\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0009": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0010": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ae64b98a7bcaa74e70025bee3df2801ee733e44878c57abb2f7fc6aac0a14020", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:65c4432c6691e14947aa3adc66d78ad2a471e601d184769b773f782d2d4a1eea", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category.\nThe <MATH_0002>-category of categories\nover <MATH_0003> has 2-fibre products.\nSuppose that\n<MATH_0004> and\n<MATH_0005> are morphisms of categories over\n<MATH_0006>.\nAn explicit 2-fibre product\n<MATH_0007> is given by the following\ndescription\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> an object of <MATH_0008> is a quadruple\n<MATH_0009>, where <MATH_0010>,\n<MATH_0011>, <MATH_0012>,\nand <MATH_0013> is an isomorphism in <MATH_0014>,\n<STRUCT_0004> a morphism <MATH_0015> is given by a pair\n<MATH_0016>, where <MATH_0017> is a morphism in <MATH_0018>, and\n<MATH_0019> is a\nmorphism in <MATH_0020> such that\n<STRUCT_0005>\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0021> and <MATH_0022> induce the same morphism <MATH_0023>, and\n<STRUCT_0007> the diagram\n<MATH_0024>\nis commutative.\n<STRUCT_0008>\n<STRUCT_0009>\nThe functors <MATH_0025>\nand <MATH_0026> are the\nforgetful functors in this case. The transformation <MATH_0027> is given on the object <MATH_0028> by\n<MATH_0029>.\n<STRUCT_0010>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7891914cbc58fa48287dc991a25a8060895716462ef47fafa79e6db5c37c44af", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:0040:lemma/0001"}, "state": "READY"}}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:d688e12535f9b12e49fa8f60d960a5002d4c4c551d7728302a3ff1aa53990d64", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p012-